# Safe startup fstab for begonia.
#
# PBRP draws its splash before processing encrypted storage. The MicroTrust
# metadata-FBE path can block in fscrypt_mount_metadata_encrypted() when the
# vendor TEE/HAL is unavailable. This diagnostic image intentionally omits
# /data and all fscrypt options; it does not wipe or modify user data.
#
# Use variant=static or dynamic with PBRP_ENABLE_CRYPTO=true only when the
# hardware-backed decryption stack has been tested for the target ROM.
#
# Layout (verified on-device against a working TWRP, Android 16 QPR2):
# begonia has no physical "super" partition. The super lives INSIDE the
# physical system partition, so by-name/system is the super *container* and
# is not a mountable filesystem (all zeros, no ext4 magic at offset 1080).
# Only by-name/vendor carries a real ext4 superblock. The mountable
# filesystems are the five dynamic (dm) devices /dev/block/mapper/*, which is
# what the ROM's own fstab mounts using the "logical" fs_mgr flag.
#
# Pointing these entries at by-name/* makes /system fail to mount outright,
# which is what left recovery wedged on the splash. Keep them "logical".
#
# <src>            <mnt_point>    <type>  <mnt_flags>   <fs_mgr_flags>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
system             /system       ext4    ro,barrier=1  wait,logical
system_ext         /system_ext   ext4    ro,barrier=1  wait,logical
product            /product      ext4    ro,barrier=1  wait,logical
vendor             /vendor       ext4    ro,barrier=1  wait,logical
odm                /odm          ext4    ro,barrier=1  wait,logical

/dev/block/platform/bootdevice/by-name/misc      /misc                 emmc     defaults                                                        defaults
/dev/block/platform/bootdevice/by-name/metadata  /metadata             ext4     noatime,nosuid,nodev,discard                                    wait,check,formattable
